  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration (config_019, acc=0.639) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder with multimodal fusion (resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile). All completed experiments have used pca_n2000; the RNA encoder dimension is completely unexplored. The image modality contributes only modestly over RNA-only (0.639 vs 0.591), suggesting the RNA representation quality is the primary performance driver. Question tested: Does a learned single-cell latent representation (scvi_n200) outperform a linear PCA projection in the best multimodal setup? This is a clean single-variable change from config_019. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder is the largest untested design axis with potentially high impact. Resolving whether a nonlinear learned encoder helps (or hurts) in the multimodal context will either open a new improvement direction or confirm PCA sufficiency, thereby reducing the effective search space for all subsequent experiments. It is more informative than re-testing aggregation (avgpool already has strong RNA-only evidence) or image encoder (resnet50 vs ViT-L showed negligible difference)."
}

